# Observed facts (evidence/remote-observations.json)
- Kobe (u24) runs 8da2075; process alive and idle since end_turn 17:13:43Z.
- Stop notice: none can run now; focus only n75,n84,n92; waiting n133; 2 blocked steps.
- Focus was set by the model at 13:20:11Z with user_requested=true after the user ASKED whether the two top items were closed. No explicit instruction to work only on them was found in that window.
- work_parallel_status three times: enabled=false, version0, no leases. work_parallel_configure/run never called.
- Router usage observations empty ({}).

# Code-confirmed mechanism
work_discovery.discovery_hint disables discovery whenever focus node_ids exist. Stop hook therefore emits only the notice; it neither continues nor asks for backlog search. Focus persists until explicit clear, so 33 other registered items stay held and Walkie backlog is never queried.

# Parallel
Not a runtime crash: feature default is off and was never enabled. Even if enabled, P2-P5 admission requires usage observations; with none, only P1 could be admitted (per existing limitation text).

# Item processing
Final focused leaves were waiting/blocked; the model's stated next action was not recorded as a runnable leaf, so actionable=0. Walkie said thread still open, the model ended turn anyway.

# Unverified
Board snapshot files were ACL-denied; exact current focus/leaf state comes from transcript notices, not direct file reads. No root cause for model misinterpretation beyond the transcript. No remote state changed, no restart, no ACL change.
